on today's menu we got an explanation  for cyberpunk 2077's lack of police  chases as well as an update on halo and  mass effect  so if you've played cyberpunk 2077 in  the past year then you may have realized  that outside of the scripted mission  sequences police never chase you in a  vehicle they also had a habit of  appearing out of thin air instead of  driving up to the scene of the crime  like in most open world games well now  2077's quest director pavel sasco spoke  about the missing feature during a  recent stream according to sasko there  wasn't enough time to make a police  chase system work before release that  mixed with technical limitations of the  engine led the team to eventually give  up on the feature and speaking of  missing features you might have also  noticed that night city's train system  didn't work however thanks to the magic  of mods now it does the cyberpunk 2077  metro system mod by neowize features 19  working stations and full integration  with the game's ui and controls and  players can switch between first and  third person views  over the weekend halo infinite had its  first big in-person professional  tournament and according to 343's  esports league tashi the event was the  most viewed halo esports event of all  time after just one day of competition  however no specific viewership numbers  were made available tashi also revealed  some competitors were using quote  development consoles due to the ongoing  semiconductor shortages on twitter tashi  said players in the open bracket will  play on series x development units which  are fundamentally identical and will run  in retail mode  in other halo news 343 industries is  aware of big team battle's matchmaking  issues and is reportedly a top priority  the issues involve players attempting to  match make into halo infinite's 12v12  multiplayer playlist frequently  receiving matchmaking errors and those  who do find a match having a high chance  of finding themselves with far fewer  teammates than normal in a forum post on  halo waypoint 343 confirms that it has  seen an increase in big team battle  matchmaking errors over the past few  days steps the team has already taken to  migrate the issue such as reducing sizes  to 10v10 and disabling the ability for  players to join in progress have not had  a meaningful impact and have been  removed 343 describes the problem as  complex because of this and the upcoming  holidays a patch to address the problem  likely won't come until 2022  so it appears the next mass effect game  will as rumored run on epic's unreal  engine bioware producer brennan holmes  recently tweeted about an open position  at the company for associate technical  director and the ideal candidate will  have experience with unreal engine 4 and  5. this doesn't flat out confirm that  the new mass effect game will run on  some form of the unreal engine however  reporter jeff grubb who was among the  first to report the next mass effect  will use the unreal engine followed up  to say that this is indeed the case and  that it's unreal engine 5 specifically  and if jeff grubb is right then that  means we might be able to steer clear of  some of the frostbite engine glitches  that made andromeda a comedy so what's  your favorite mass effect game let me  know in the comments below  later  [Music]
 

